1
00:00:05,305 --> 00:00:07,307
I want Mariko to smile.

2
00:00:08,908 --> 00:00:10,010
That's all.

3
00:00:10,710 --> 00:00:12,345
She's in the way.

4
00:00:12,412 --> 00:00:14,047
She's just like her mother.

5
00:00:14,114 --> 00:00:14,781
NOZAWA CONSTRUCTION

6
00:00:14,848 --> 00:00:15,882
It was you, wasn't it?

7
00:00:16,816 --> 00:00:18,084
You're the one who killed Tateiwa.

8
00:00:18,151 --> 00:00:21,721
I wonder how everyone would feel
if they found out who you really are.

9
00:00:21,788 --> 00:00:23,490
I wonder what Mariko would think too.

10
00:01:04,197 --> 00:01:08,835
‎TAISUKE SAKURA

11
00:01:41,501 --> 00:01:42,569
Is this you?

12
00:01:47,006 --> 00:01:49,209
You've been following
my social media for years,

13
00:01:50,009 --> 00:01:52,445
before we even met?

14
00:01:54,914 --> 00:01:57,550
What? What does this mean?

15
00:02:01,721 --> 00:02:02,555
Well…

16
00:02:11,698 --> 00:02:12,732
Up until now…

17
00:02:15,101 --> 00:02:17,837
I just thought you were someone
who happened to share my interests.

18
00:02:18,505 --> 00:02:21,307
Visiting cafes is one of my hobbies.

19
00:02:21,808 --> 00:02:24,043
I'm a huge Marvel fan.

20
00:02:24,110 --> 00:02:25,578
You somehow

21
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:29,315
always appear when I want you to.

22
00:02:31,584 --> 00:02:34,387
You say things like
you've known me forever.

23
00:02:35,388 --> 00:02:37,190
I always thought
you were a strange person.

24
00:02:38,358 --> 00:02:39,192
But…

25
00:02:40,493 --> 00:02:44,531
So none of that was a coincidence?

26
00:02:45,365 --> 00:02:47,500
You were looking into me ahead of time?

27
00:02:53,706 --> 00:02:56,109
Hey, say something!

28
00:02:58,745 --> 00:02:59,579
I'm sorry.

29
00:03:02,815 --> 00:03:03,850
You're sorry…

30
00:03:11,391 --> 00:03:13,092
Mariko, please wait.

31
00:03:14,661 --> 00:03:15,662
Mariko.

32
00:03:26,239 --> 00:03:27,106
I'm sorry.

33
00:04:18,625 --> 00:04:19,525
Yukimura.

34
00:04:26,866 --> 00:04:28,668
An incident has occurred,

35
00:04:29,235 --> 00:04:32,171
and someone who looked like you
was caught on the dashcam

36
00:04:32,972 --> 00:04:34,907
of a car parked near the scene.

37
00:04:36,776 --> 00:04:38,511
We would like to ask you some questions.

38
00:04:38,578 --> 00:04:40,580
Could you please
accompany us to the station?

39
00:04:43,016 --> 00:04:44,117
What kind of incident?

40
00:04:52,091 --> 00:04:52,959
Step over here.

41
00:05:03,670 --> 00:05:05,405
Sayuri Nose…

42
00:05:08,875 --> 00:05:10,243
has been found dead.

43
00:05:18,818 --> 00:05:21,154
FATHER

44
00:05:47,046 --> 00:05:48,247
This

45
00:05:49,382 --> 00:05:52,752
shows you and Sayuri Nose
entering the alley.

46
00:05:54,087 --> 00:05:55,121
And this one

47
00:05:55,888 --> 00:05:59,992
shows the person who first discovered
the scene entering the alley.

48
00:06:01,361 --> 00:06:04,130
During this gap, Sayuri Nose was murdered.

49
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:09,635
The circumstantial evidence is complete.

50
00:06:09,702 --> 00:06:11,104
-Why…
-Hm?

51
00:06:13,339 --> 00:06:15,641
No, I mean,
why does it line up so perfectly?

52
00:06:16,776 --> 00:06:18,845
You were present at the scene

53
00:06:19,779 --> 00:06:23,383
of two murders,
Tateiwa's and Sayuri Nose's.

54
00:06:23,449 --> 00:06:28,054
I don't believe those can be seen
as mere coincidences.

55
00:06:33,626 --> 00:06:34,827
Is the world…

56
00:06:36,763 --> 00:06:39,766
really so full of coincidences?

57
00:06:41,167 --> 00:06:44,470
Much like your relationship
with Mariko Nose.

58
00:06:47,273 --> 00:06:48,207
What are you talking about?

59
00:06:48,741 --> 00:06:50,309
You and Mariko

60
00:06:51,210 --> 00:06:52,812
went to the same middle school,

61
00:06:53,513 --> 00:06:54,347
high school,

62
00:06:55,615 --> 00:06:57,417
university,

63
00:06:58,584 --> 00:07:00,853
and now are working at the same company.

64
00:07:02,822 --> 00:07:03,689
Yes.

65
00:07:04,290 --> 00:07:07,026
You say this is all a coincidence?

66
00:07:08,895 --> 00:07:11,831
Does this have anything to do
with Sayuri being murdered?

67
00:07:13,466 --> 00:07:16,702
It is an important piece
in proving your motive.

68
00:07:27,713 --> 00:07:32,485
To answer your previous question,
I don't think so.

69
00:07:36,355 --> 00:07:39,258
Coincidences don't just happen
that easily.

70
00:07:41,027 --> 00:07:44,697
Everything that seems like a coincidence
usually has some intent behind it.

71
00:07:46,332 --> 00:07:48,868
Sometimes, people wish
it was a coincidence,

72
00:07:50,269 --> 00:07:52,238
or people fail to see the hidden reason

73
00:07:52,305 --> 00:07:54,340
and assume something happened
just because.

74
00:07:58,578 --> 00:08:01,147
The fact that I was present
at two murder scenes…

75
00:08:02,081 --> 00:08:03,249
I think it was also due

76
00:08:04,784 --> 00:08:07,887
to someone's intention,

77
00:08:09,222 --> 00:08:12,124
someone pulling the strings.

78
00:08:16,395 --> 00:08:17,663
Really?

79
00:08:20,333 --> 00:08:21,267
Who could it be?

80
00:08:24,170 --> 00:08:25,771
I'd like to know that myself.

81
00:08:39,051 --> 00:08:40,653
Um, uh,

82
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:45,858
so in other words, you did
what you did to protect Mariko,

83
00:08:45,925 --> 00:08:49,428
-Tateiwa, and Sayuri, right?
-Yes.

84
00:08:50,062 --> 00:08:52,832
You dug up dirt on those two
and threatened them.

85
00:08:53,399 --> 00:08:55,935
Yes. I swear to God, that's all I did.

86
00:08:56,502 --> 00:08:58,604
Man, that's already problematic enough.

87
00:08:59,539 --> 00:09:02,041
-I'm sorry.
-Why are you apologizing to me?

88
00:09:02,875 --> 00:09:03,910
Sorry…

89
00:09:08,381 --> 00:09:10,216
There's too much stuff to think about.

90
00:09:10,850 --> 00:09:12,351
First off,

91
00:09:12,418 --> 00:09:14,754
Mariko found out
about your account, right?

92
00:09:15,955 --> 00:09:17,223
I guess it freaked her out?

93
00:09:21,861 --> 00:09:24,096
Hm, probably…

94
00:09:25,031 --> 00:09:26,532
And during that,

95
00:09:26,599 --> 00:09:29,335
the police took you in for questioning,
right in front of her.

96
00:09:32,872 --> 00:09:35,141
No, no, it's fine!

97
00:09:35,207 --> 00:09:37,143
If you explain it, she'll understand.

98
00:09:37,209 --> 00:09:39,111
It's impossible. I can't explain it.

99
00:09:39,178 --> 00:09:40,580
But you have to.

100
00:09:41,380 --> 00:09:44,850
You don't want to lose
your 25-year love, do you?

101
00:09:46,752 --> 00:09:50,423
But it's impossible.

102
00:09:55,761 --> 00:09:57,063
Why were you following her?

103
00:09:59,966 --> 00:10:00,800
What?

104
00:10:01,701 --> 00:10:04,103
You could have used a different account
or just lurked without following.

105
00:10:04,737 --> 00:10:07,573
You didn't have to go,
"Oh, a new post! Like!"

106
00:10:09,809 --> 00:10:13,346
I knew about Mariko's social media account
right when she created it.

107
00:10:13,913 --> 00:10:17,416
But I thought it'd be bad to follow her
right away, so I waited for a few months.

108
00:10:18,884 --> 00:10:22,388
At first, I was afraid
that if a stranger followed her,

109
00:10:22,455 --> 00:10:23,923
she'd be creeped out.

110
00:10:25,024 --> 00:10:27,093
But getting to hear
Mariko's inner thoughts,

111
00:10:27,159 --> 00:10:30,196
which I never could have known before,
expressed directly by her,

112
00:10:30,262 --> 00:10:31,631
it was an unbelievable experience.

113
00:10:32,198 --> 00:10:34,667
And being able to reply with a "like"…

114
00:10:36,636 --> 00:10:38,571
Mariko seeing my "like"…

115
00:10:39,972 --> 00:10:42,475
It was just incredible.

116
00:10:44,644 --> 00:10:49,248
And before I knew it, I was liking

117
00:10:49,315 --> 00:10:51,317
every single post she made…

118
00:10:53,653 --> 00:10:54,520
I'm sorry.

119
00:10:54,587 --> 00:10:56,288
I told you, don't apologize to me.

120
00:10:58,758 --> 00:10:59,625
Well, whatever.

121
00:11:00,593 --> 00:11:01,661
More importantly, the issue now is--

122
00:11:01,727 --> 00:11:03,462
Is Mariko okay?

123
00:11:03,529 --> 00:11:06,132
Huh? Even at a time like this,
that's what you're worried about?

124
00:11:06,932 --> 00:11:11,003
Those two were clearly
showing hostility toward her.

125
00:11:12,338 --> 00:11:14,340
What was the reason they were killed?

126
00:11:15,908 --> 00:11:17,677
What if the killer's target is Mariko?

127
00:11:37,730 --> 00:11:44,637
LEARN MORE ABOUT SLEEP

128
00:11:44,704 --> 00:11:45,905
-Oh…
-Here.

129
00:11:45,971 --> 00:11:46,906
Thank you.

130
00:11:55,781 --> 00:11:56,782
Keito.

131
00:12:11,263 --> 00:12:12,198
Father.

132
00:12:27,947 --> 00:12:30,282
Earlier today around six a.m.,

133
00:12:30,349 --> 00:12:34,120
a woman was reported lying prone
on the riverbank

134
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:38,124
under an elevated structure
in Setagaya Ward.

135
00:12:38,858 --> 00:12:41,794
The deceased has been identified
as Sayuri Nose,

136
00:12:41,861 --> 00:12:45,097
wife of Ginjiro Nose,
president of major cosmetics firm

137
00:12:45,164 --> 00:12:46,398
Nose Cosmetics.

138
00:12:47,266 --> 00:12:50,402
Marks suggesting strangulation
were found on Sayuri's neck,

139
00:12:50,469 --> 00:12:54,006
and police are investigating
the case as a homicide.

140
00:12:54,507 --> 00:12:57,409
Regarding Nose Cosmetics, one month ago…

141
00:12:58,744 --> 00:13:03,482
So that's why Mariko was absent yesterday.

142
00:13:04,617 --> 00:13:07,286
Isn't this insane? Like, seriously scary.

143
00:13:09,588 --> 00:13:12,491
-Good morning.
-Mariko…

144
00:13:21,667 --> 00:13:25,571
I'm sorry for causing
everyone such concern.

145
00:13:27,006 --> 00:13:29,341
And for taking a sudden day off yesterday.

146
00:13:29,408 --> 00:13:31,877
-Mariko, you don't need to apologize.
-I mean,

147
00:13:31,944 --> 00:13:33,679
-what's the situation actually like?
-Stop.

148
00:13:34,413 --> 00:13:35,548
Ah, it's fine.

149
00:13:36,248 --> 00:13:39,351
But honestly, we haven't been told
much more than what's on the news either.

150
00:13:40,019 --> 00:13:43,022
Mariko, you can take today off too.

151
00:13:43,756 --> 00:13:44,890
I can't do that.

152
00:13:45,624 --> 00:13:49,028
Besides, the internal company presentation
is soon. We need to hurry and prepare.

153
00:13:49,695 --> 00:13:50,896
-Yes.
-Yes.

154
00:13:51,564 --> 00:13:53,098
Thank you all.

155
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:55,734
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

156
00:13:57,469 --> 00:14:00,873
Hashimoto, for the 3 p.m.
promotional strategy meeting…

157
00:14:00,940 --> 00:14:04,310
Eleven through three are promising,

158
00:14:05,611 --> 00:14:08,781
-but with 11…
-Uh, regarding number six…

159
00:14:08,848 --> 00:14:10,216
There could be 1.58 million…

160
00:14:10,783 --> 00:14:13,319
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

161
00:14:25,064 --> 00:14:25,965
Mariko.

162
00:14:27,399 --> 00:14:31,537
Um, about what happened
the day before yesterday…

163
00:14:31,604 --> 00:14:32,938
Sorry, but…

164
00:14:34,206 --> 00:14:35,608
too much has been happening.

165
00:14:35,674 --> 00:14:37,076
My mind is a mess right now.

166
00:14:37,943 --> 00:14:39,378
I don't want to think about anything.

167
00:14:42,915 --> 00:14:44,049
I'm sorry.

168
00:15:06,572 --> 00:15:08,274
My 32 years of life

169
00:15:08,941 --> 00:15:11,443
were short, but fulfilling.

170
00:15:12,378 --> 00:15:13,312
Mariko.

171
00:15:14,113 --> 00:15:15,147
Please stay well.

172
00:15:15,814 --> 00:15:19,051
Walk over my fallen body
and find happiness.

173
00:15:23,022 --> 00:15:25,090
The higher-ups said it was suicide.

174
00:15:25,157 --> 00:15:27,860
We can't do anything after that.

175
00:15:30,462 --> 00:15:33,532
No, I can't die yet.

176
00:15:38,938 --> 00:15:40,572
Even if I am to die,

177
00:15:41,140 --> 00:15:43,676
it'll be after I've ensured
Mariko's safety and happiness.

178
00:15:56,388 --> 00:15:57,923
Um, excuse me.

179
00:15:59,692 --> 00:16:02,194
Why did you put those flowers there?

180
00:16:03,796 --> 00:16:09,401
A long time ago, a regular customer
of my shop had an accident here.

181
00:16:09,969 --> 00:16:11,136
Your shop…

182
00:16:12,004 --> 00:16:14,606
I run a flower shop nearby.

183
00:16:17,209 --> 00:16:19,712
It's a white flower about this big!

184
00:16:19,778 --> 00:16:20,779
Is it this one?

185
00:16:20,846 --> 00:16:23,415
No, not that. A white one, about this big…

186
00:16:32,257 --> 00:16:34,593
FUSAIDO FLOWER SHOP

187
00:16:34,660 --> 00:16:35,995
You know who the culprit might be?

188
00:16:36,795 --> 00:16:37,629
Yes.

189
00:16:38,697 --> 00:16:40,099
My daughter Mariko was the victim

190
00:16:40,165 --> 00:16:42,634
of an attempted kidnapping
when she was little.

191
00:16:45,371 --> 00:16:47,206
The Satoru Hatano case, right?

192
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:52,511
I was still a university student
back then, but I remember the case well.

193
00:16:53,212 --> 00:16:56,515
I suspect that both Tateiwa and my wife

194
00:16:57,383 --> 00:17:00,352
were killed by this man, Hatano.

195
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:05,791
Actually, I haven't been able to contact
my secretary, Asai, for a while.

196
00:17:07,126 --> 00:17:09,094
I've been receiving emails
from him, though.

197
00:17:10,562 --> 00:17:14,500
His mother back home is doing fine.

198
00:17:14,566 --> 00:17:16,535
Asai hasn't returned there.

199
00:17:18,470 --> 00:17:21,006
Also, this was left on his desk.

200
00:17:22,741 --> 00:17:25,978
It seems to belong
to the editor of this article.

201
00:17:26,045 --> 00:17:30,249
Hatano must be involved
in Asai's disappearance.

202
00:17:32,251 --> 00:17:33,886
I understand the situation.

203
00:17:34,987 --> 00:17:36,588
I will take action on my end.

204
00:17:37,322 --> 00:17:38,457
Thank you very much.

205
00:17:40,659 --> 00:17:41,994
Please stop.

206
00:17:42,061 --> 00:17:44,096
SETAGAYA CASE

207
00:17:44,163 --> 00:17:46,832
You must also be worried
about Mariko's safety.

208
00:17:52,938 --> 00:17:54,740
Leave it to me.

209
00:18:01,680 --> 00:18:06,752
I don't know anything about that.

210
00:18:09,488 --> 00:18:12,157
You've been a secretary
at that company for 25 years.

211
00:18:12,224 --> 00:18:13,759
There's no way you don't know.

212
00:18:13,826 --> 00:18:16,061
No, I really don't.

213
00:18:17,162 --> 00:18:18,831
Useless.

214
00:18:18,897 --> 00:18:21,133
No point in keeping you alive then.

215
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:23,969
What are you planning to do?

216
00:18:26,438 --> 00:18:30,309
Well, you see, I want to meet him.

217
00:18:30,375 --> 00:18:34,847
You can't just alter someone's life
and never meet them face to face, right?

218
00:18:35,914 --> 00:18:37,583
If it wasn't for that kid,

219
00:18:38,117 --> 00:18:40,185
I wouldn't have been caught.

220
00:18:41,053 --> 00:18:44,056
I need to give a proper
token of appreciation

221
00:18:44,923 --> 00:18:49,461
to that brave young boy
who saved the little princess.

222
00:18:58,670 --> 00:19:02,441
Hello? Yes, that's right.

223
00:19:02,508 --> 00:19:04,276
I'll pay the money.

224
00:19:04,343 --> 00:19:06,845
Yukimura, I need to talk to you.

225
00:19:07,346 --> 00:19:08,247
Yes?

226
00:19:10,015 --> 00:19:11,750
Yukimura, you are

227
00:19:12,317 --> 00:19:14,153
that boy who saved Mariko
back then, right?

228
00:19:14,887 --> 00:19:16,855
Years ago, on behalf of the president,

229
00:19:16,922 --> 00:19:19,057
I visited your parents
to express our gratitude.

230
00:19:20,826 --> 00:19:22,327
Could you keep this a secret?

231
00:19:23,362 --> 00:19:25,497
I don't want Mariko to find out.

232
00:19:25,564 --> 00:19:26,532
Please.

233
00:19:38,210 --> 00:19:40,679
SETAGAYA KIDNAPPING CASE DETAILS

234
00:19:46,151 --> 00:19:47,786
MARIKO NOSE - ELEMENTARY SCHOOL STUDENT

235
00:19:47,853 --> 00:19:50,489
ALMOST TAKEN AWAY BY A STRANGER

236
00:19:50,556 --> 00:19:51,623
SHE SCREAMED FOR SOMEONE TO HELP

237
00:19:54,593 --> 00:19:57,062
COLOR OF THE VEHICLE WAS BLACK

238
00:20:00,165 --> 00:20:03,068
SOTA YUKIMURA - ELEMENTARY SCHOOL STUDENT

239
00:20:30,596 --> 00:20:33,465
Excuse me. Here's this month's sales data.

240
00:20:33,532 --> 00:20:35,400
-Please check it.
-Okay.

241
00:21:01,059 --> 00:21:01,960
-Sorry.
-I'm sorry.

242
00:21:02,928 --> 00:21:05,197
Please check this.

243
00:21:05,764 --> 00:21:06,632
Okay.

244
00:21:09,735 --> 00:21:15,674
Which type of plastic
would be best for this?

245
00:21:19,945 --> 00:21:23,515
For that, recycled PET would be best.

246
00:21:25,317 --> 00:21:27,119
Recycled PET?

247
00:21:28,620 --> 00:21:31,390
Well, biomass plastic
is also an attractive choice,

248
00:21:31,456 --> 00:21:33,792
but it might be more difficult to manage.

249
00:21:34,459 --> 00:21:37,296
I think recycled PET, which has
a proven record, would be best,

250
00:21:37,362 --> 00:21:38,664
considering our schedule.

251
00:21:39,231 --> 00:21:40,198
I see.

252
00:21:40,265 --> 00:21:42,668
Well, it looks good for sustainability.

253
00:21:42,734 --> 00:21:44,369
It doesn't really give off a luxury feel.

254
00:21:44,436 --> 00:21:47,673
Okay then, for example,
instead of 100% recycled PET,

255
00:21:47,739 --> 00:21:51,476
-we could use 30%.
-Yeah, I see.

256
00:22:13,465 --> 00:22:14,499
Mariko.

257
00:22:15,867 --> 00:22:19,538
I want to talk about
what happened the other day.

258
00:22:21,773 --> 00:22:24,643
Do you have time after this?

259
00:22:44,930 --> 00:22:47,065
What are you doing here? What happened?

260
00:22:47,132 --> 00:22:48,400
Are you finished with work?

261
00:22:49,568 --> 00:22:50,502
Yes.

262
00:22:50,569 --> 00:22:51,570
I'll give you a ride.

263
00:22:52,137 --> 00:22:53,004
‎What?

264
00:22:53,071 --> 00:22:55,974
I'll explain the details later. Come on.

265
00:23:18,263 --> 00:23:19,798
Asai is missing?

266
00:23:21,032 --> 00:23:23,068
It hasn't been definitively
confirmed yet, but…

267
00:23:23,702 --> 00:23:26,238
Is it the same person
who got Tateiwa and Sayuri?

268
00:23:28,707 --> 00:23:30,575
We can't rule out the possibility.

269
00:23:31,276 --> 00:23:34,513
However, though I cannot share details,

270
00:23:34,579 --> 00:23:36,615
the police hold a different view.

271
00:23:39,851 --> 00:23:40,719
Mariko.

272
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:44,189
When we went to the art museum
together recently,

273
00:23:44,756 --> 00:23:46,358
Yukimura was there too.

274
00:23:49,995 --> 00:23:55,133
Is Yukimura stalking you?

275
00:23:57,235 --> 00:23:58,437
Is there anything that comes to mind?

276
00:24:00,605 --> 00:24:01,740
Ah, good morning.

277
00:24:01,807 --> 00:24:03,942
Would you like
to walk to the station together?

278
00:24:05,210 --> 00:24:06,144
Mariko…

279
00:24:10,148 --> 00:24:11,316
There is, right?

280
00:24:15,854 --> 00:24:17,055
It's okay.

281
00:24:19,491 --> 00:24:21,493
I will protect you, Mariko.

282
00:25:05,270 --> 00:25:06,538
-Goodbye.
-Good day.

283
00:25:48,380 --> 00:25:51,650
I found a nice Italian place
the other day.

284
00:25:52,150 --> 00:25:54,886
-Would you like to go sometime?
-Let's see…

285
00:26:03,995 --> 00:26:04,963
Thank you, everyone.

286
00:26:05,764 --> 00:26:07,132
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

287
00:26:07,999 --> 00:26:10,268
Isn't that detective
mixing business with pleasure?

288
00:26:10,335 --> 00:26:12,270
He's been by Mariko's side
non-stop these past few days.

289
00:26:12,337 --> 00:26:16,107
Well, it's not a normal situation,
so I get wanting to be cautious, but…

290
00:26:38,964 --> 00:26:40,665
Thank you, everyone.

291
00:26:40,732 --> 00:26:42,334
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

292
00:26:42,400 --> 00:26:44,869
You should be the one
walking her home, Yukimura.

293
00:26:44,936 --> 00:26:46,671
What are you doing?

294
00:26:47,405 --> 00:26:49,507
Seriously, why are you just zoning out?

295
00:26:53,144 --> 00:26:54,980
No, I didn't say anything.

296
00:26:56,014 --> 00:26:58,383
It's totally obvious. Right?

297
00:26:58,450 --> 00:27:00,719
Yes. It's super easy to see.

298
00:27:01,419 --> 00:27:02,821
What's gotten into you lately?

299
00:27:03,922 --> 00:27:05,924
She hates me now…

300
00:27:06,758 --> 00:27:08,960
-That's what happened.
-What?

301
00:27:09,728 --> 00:27:10,895
Sorry.

302
00:27:27,345 --> 00:27:31,316
Lately, a lot of skincare products
for men have been coming out.

303
00:27:32,751 --> 00:27:34,285
Thanks to your influence, Mariko,

304
00:27:34,352 --> 00:27:36,655
I've started noticing those things too.

305
00:27:37,956 --> 00:27:40,125
-Back when I was young--
-Sakura.

306
00:27:41,893 --> 00:27:42,727
Yes?

307
00:27:46,064 --> 00:27:49,334
You don't need to accompany me
to work anymore.

308
00:27:54,539 --> 00:27:56,274
About what we talked about the other day…

309
00:27:57,542 --> 00:28:00,645
I agree with you that Yukimura

310
00:28:01,446 --> 00:28:05,316
has been acting a bit strangely.

311
00:28:06,651 --> 00:28:10,121
I feel a sense of discomfort,
wondering what on earth he's doing.

312
00:28:12,323 --> 00:28:13,425
But…

313
00:28:14,893 --> 00:28:17,929
he wouldn't kill anyone.

314
00:28:19,164 --> 00:28:20,365
He's not that kind of person.

315
00:28:25,136 --> 00:28:26,104
‎Is that so?

316
00:28:52,530 --> 00:28:54,032
MARIKO NOSE - DAUGHTER

317
00:28:54,099 --> 00:28:54,933
Sakura.

318
00:28:55,800 --> 00:28:58,737
Here are the tracking results
for Asai's smartphone that you asked for.

319
00:28:58,803 --> 00:28:59,704
Thank you.

320
00:29:07,545 --> 00:29:11,883
SOTA YUKIMURA

321
00:29:12,951 --> 00:29:14,786
FUNERAL OF SAYURI NOSE

322
00:29:14,853 --> 00:29:20,191
Here, O Sariputra, form is emptiness
And the very emptiness is form

323
00:29:20,258 --> 00:29:23,595
Emptiness does not differ from form
Form does not differ from emptiness

324
00:29:23,661 --> 00:29:26,131
Whatever is emptiness, that is form

325
00:29:26,197 --> 00:29:31,770
Same is true of feelings, perceptions
Impulses, and consciousness

326
00:29:31,836 --> 00:29:34,672
Here, O Sariputra
All dharmas are marked with emptiness

327
00:29:35,340 --> 00:29:37,242
They are not produced or stopped

328
00:29:37,308 --> 00:29:39,043
Not defiled or immaculate
Not deficient or complete

329
00:29:39,110 --> 00:29:41,613
Therefore, O Sariputra
In emptiness there is no form nor feeling

330
00:29:41,679 --> 00:29:44,182
Nor perception, nor impulse
Nor consciousness…

331
00:29:44,249 --> 00:29:46,918
I wonder why Yukimura didn't make it.

332
00:29:46,985 --> 00:29:47,952
RECEPTION

333
00:29:48,019 --> 00:29:50,488
Does Mariko not like him that much?

334
00:29:50,555 --> 00:29:51,990
I wonder what he did.

335
00:29:59,330 --> 00:30:01,332
-Ah…
-Ah, Izumi.

336
00:30:01,399 --> 00:30:02,467
What's up?

337
00:30:02,534 --> 00:30:05,537
Well, I figured this must be tough,
so take these if you'd like.

338
00:30:06,504 --> 00:30:07,572
Thank you.

339
00:30:11,509 --> 00:30:13,378
-Also, sorry to ask…
-Hm?

340
00:30:13,444 --> 00:30:15,146
-Could I use the toilet here?
-Yes.

341
00:30:15,880 --> 00:30:17,482
-That way, on the right.
-Thank you.

342
00:30:27,525 --> 00:30:30,161
Keito. Why don't you go
get something to eat?

343
00:30:45,443 --> 00:30:46,377
Sis…

344
00:30:47,812 --> 00:30:48,646
Hm?

345
00:30:51,015 --> 00:30:52,684
I accidentally overheard something.

346
00:30:55,920 --> 00:30:57,388
A while before the incident,

347
00:30:58,790 --> 00:31:01,559
Mom and Dad were talking at home.

348
00:31:01,626 --> 00:31:04,095
The one who will succeed me is Mariko.

349
00:31:04,162 --> 00:31:05,864
You haven't forgotten, have you?

350
00:31:06,831 --> 00:31:10,335
That you and I share the same secret.

351
00:31:14,339 --> 00:31:15,807
The same secret?

352
00:31:16,941 --> 00:31:20,044
Were they doing something bad?

353
00:31:20,812 --> 00:31:23,214
Is that why this happened?

354
00:31:28,987 --> 00:31:35,159
FUNERAL

355
00:31:48,206 --> 00:31:49,340
Yukimura.

356
00:31:57,715 --> 00:31:58,616
Could you please

357
00:32:00,251 --> 00:32:02,654
stop approaching Mariko?

358
00:32:04,322 --> 00:32:05,657
Why is a detective saying that?

359
00:32:05,723 --> 00:32:08,760
Because I have to protect her from you.

360
00:32:10,328 --> 00:32:12,764
I could arrest you.

361
00:32:14,332 --> 00:32:18,536
What you are doing is stalking.

362
00:32:20,939 --> 00:32:21,973
Normally, it requires that

363
00:32:22,573 --> 00:32:26,311
the other party be aware
they are being followed,

364
00:32:26,377 --> 00:32:30,548
but if the conduct is judged objectively
to cause anxiety,

365
00:32:30,615 --> 00:32:32,617
it can fall under "stalking",

366
00:32:34,218 --> 00:32:36,287
even if the other party is unaware.

367
00:32:37,922 --> 00:32:38,923
In other words,

368
00:32:40,258 --> 00:32:42,727
regardless of what Mariko thinks,

369
00:32:44,395 --> 00:32:45,763
you can be punished.

370
00:32:49,334 --> 00:32:51,035
Since what age?

371
00:32:52,203 --> 00:32:57,775
You have been continually committing
criminal acts all this time.

372
00:33:00,244 --> 00:33:01,079
Am I wrong?

373
00:33:07,652 --> 00:33:08,786
-I…
-Hm?

374
00:33:11,356 --> 00:33:13,157
You didn't intend to?

375
00:33:15,360 --> 00:33:20,298
Most people who commit crimes
probably didn't intend to,

376
00:33:21,466 --> 00:33:22,867
either.

377
00:33:27,005 --> 00:33:30,141
A life ruined by a brief impulse.

378
00:33:31,476 --> 00:33:34,278
Other than that,
it was a completely stainless life.

379
00:33:39,150 --> 00:33:40,885
If only you hadn't loved her…

380
00:33:43,121 --> 00:33:45,523
you wouldn't have ended up a criminal.

381
00:33:57,869 --> 00:34:00,671
What's with that detective?
Calling you a stalker.

382
00:34:01,272 --> 00:34:04,776
It's not like
you forced yourself on Mariko.

383
00:34:05,576 --> 00:34:07,645
But it was something
I shouldn't have done.

384
00:34:11,182 --> 00:34:13,951
Besides, you've been protecting
Mariko all this time, right?

385
00:34:14,852 --> 00:34:16,754
Which is why you ended up a suspect.

386
00:34:16,821 --> 00:34:17,655
It's fine.

387
00:34:18,823 --> 00:34:21,059
It's what I chose to do.

388
00:34:23,528 --> 00:34:26,063
Besides, from Mariko's perspective,
I really am creepy.

389
00:34:28,232 --> 00:34:30,234
So this situation
is just an effect of that.

390
00:34:32,036 --> 00:34:33,371
-But still…
-It's fine.

391
00:34:40,044 --> 00:34:41,312
Yes, you're okay.

392
00:34:42,346 --> 00:34:44,048
Don't fall asleep! Take off your shoes.

393
00:34:45,049 --> 00:34:47,552
-Take them off.
-Do it yourself.

394
00:34:47,618 --> 00:34:49,787
-You're fine like that?
-Yes, cover me, please.

395
00:34:49,854 --> 00:34:50,788
-Okay.
-Thanks.

396
00:34:55,193 --> 00:34:57,428
You know you can't hold your liquor…

397
00:35:37,835 --> 00:35:39,170
PICTURE DIARY

398
00:35:55,920 --> 00:35:59,724
The President has decided
to delay the launch event.

399
00:36:00,591 --> 00:36:04,662
Then it won't
make it in time for the release.

400
00:36:04,729 --> 00:36:06,531
I won't let everyone's
hard work go to waste.

401
00:36:07,298 --> 00:36:08,699
I will protect it.

402
00:36:09,634 --> 00:36:11,269
All right, let's do it!

403
00:36:12,770 --> 00:36:14,505
-Let's do it, shall we?
-Yes.

404
00:36:14,572 --> 00:36:15,406
Thank you.

405
00:36:19,577 --> 00:36:20,978
Hello.

406
00:36:25,349 --> 00:36:29,520
I told them that, but will
we really be able to release it?

407
00:36:30,288 --> 00:36:32,256
What if we can't…

408
00:36:34,358 --> 00:36:35,860
It's rare for you to be like this.

409
00:36:39,163 --> 00:36:45,136
I thought I had a pretty lucky life.

410
00:36:48,839 --> 00:36:50,641
But maybe I was wrong?

411
00:36:58,816 --> 00:36:59,817
2 MARIKO NOSE

412
00:36:59,884 --> 00:37:01,552
No way, I beat Nose!

413
00:37:01,619 --> 00:37:03,421
-Yay!
-Yay!

414
00:37:03,487 --> 00:37:05,623
Look, look. I got 873.

415
00:37:05,690 --> 00:37:06,991
Amazing.

416
00:37:07,058 --> 00:37:08,292
-That's nuts.
-You worked hard.

417
00:37:48,799 --> 00:37:51,335
It's a good product, so if we
launch it, customers will follow.

418
00:37:51,402 --> 00:37:52,270
Yukimura.

419
00:37:53,004 --> 00:37:55,840
It's got to be now, for the sake
of the company's turnaround.

420
00:37:55,906 --> 00:37:57,875
-You're causing trouble…
-I understand how you feel,

421
00:37:58,376 --> 00:37:59,644
but now is not the time.

422
00:38:01,812 --> 00:38:03,314
There's meaning in us
pioneering and deploying this

423
00:38:03,381 --> 00:38:05,883
before other companies
release similar products.

424
00:38:05,950 --> 00:38:07,118
Please.

425
00:38:10,621 --> 00:38:11,589
‎Hey.

426
00:38:12,823 --> 00:38:14,058
-What are you doing?
-Manager…

427
00:38:15,293 --> 00:38:16,227
Come here.

428
00:38:22,867 --> 00:38:23,834
Uh, Mariko…

429
00:38:29,473 --> 00:38:30,708
What are you doing?

430
00:38:32,143 --> 00:38:32,977
Seriously,

431
00:38:34,145 --> 00:38:35,880
what is going on? What is your intention?

432
00:38:37,014 --> 00:38:37,848
I'm sorry.

433
00:38:41,419 --> 00:38:44,689
Have you always been sneaking around
doing things behind my back like this?

434
00:38:46,624 --> 00:38:48,059
Doing things on your own

435
00:38:48,125 --> 00:38:50,861
without my knowledge,
claiming it was for me?

436
00:38:57,968 --> 00:38:59,670
I always thought it was strange.

437
00:39:04,475 --> 00:39:07,011
The four-leaf clover left for me…

438
00:39:09,747 --> 00:39:13,417
The adhesive bandage
during the summer festival.

439
00:39:19,690 --> 00:39:20,591
Was that what it was?

440
00:39:24,895 --> 00:39:26,897
Whenever things weren't going well for me,

441
00:39:27,765 --> 00:39:29,100
or when bad things happened,

442
00:39:30,101 --> 00:39:33,070
assuming I might be feeling down
and acting ahead of time…

443
00:39:33,137 --> 00:39:35,473
-Was that what you were doing?
-No…

444
00:39:36,407 --> 00:39:38,442
That's just creepy!

445
00:39:38,509 --> 00:39:39,977
All of it is creepy!

446
00:39:41,445 --> 00:39:43,848
Your excessive kindness,

447
00:39:44,548 --> 00:39:47,318
your consideration,
all of it is out of line!

448
00:39:52,823 --> 00:39:56,594
When did I ever ask you to protect me?

449
00:40:04,034 --> 00:40:05,169
Don't you decide

450
00:40:06,604 --> 00:40:09,940
what's for my sake
or what my happiness is!

451
00:40:13,511 --> 00:40:14,345
I'm sorry.

452
00:40:17,882 --> 00:40:18,749
I won't forgive you.

453
00:40:22,119 --> 00:40:24,488
If you leave my side,
I will never forgive you!

454
00:40:28,292 --> 00:40:29,226
I will never…

455
00:40:31,962 --> 00:40:32,963
forgive you.

456
00:40:56,921 --> 00:40:59,156
From Mariko's perspective,
I really am creepy.

457
00:41:00,558 --> 00:41:02,493
So this situation
is just an effect of that.

458
00:41:03,461 --> 00:41:04,662
-But still…
-It's fine.

459
00:41:07,398 --> 00:41:11,802
I just want Mariko to smile and be happy.

460
00:41:17,007 --> 00:41:19,410
I kept thinking about
what I could do for her…

461
00:41:22,246 --> 00:41:24,682
but me disappearing
is what's best for Mariko.

462
00:41:32,289 --> 00:41:35,025
That's how I can protect
Mariko's happiness.

463
00:42:21,038 --> 00:42:21,972
Here you go.

464
00:42:24,008 --> 00:42:24,909
Thank you!

465
00:42:28,913 --> 00:42:29,847
Mom!

466
00:42:31,982 --> 00:42:34,151
Oh, Mariko, welcome back!

467
00:42:40,958 --> 00:42:41,792
Here.

468
00:42:43,928 --> 00:42:45,896
Thank you!

469
00:42:46,931 --> 00:42:48,766
-You got these for me?
-Yes!

470
00:42:50,167 --> 00:42:51,302
So pretty.

471
00:42:52,570 --> 00:42:53,470
Wanna go home?

472
00:42:55,406 --> 00:42:56,941
Did you walk here alone?

473
00:42:57,007 --> 00:43:00,077
-Yes, that's right.
-Wow, that's amazing.

474
00:43:52,329 --> 00:43:53,797
You bastard.

475
00:43:53,864 --> 00:43:59,269
You take advantage
when people try to be nice to you!

476
00:44:12,650 --> 00:44:14,852
If you don't know anything,

477
00:44:14,918 --> 00:44:17,154
there's no point in keeping you alive.

478
00:44:20,190 --> 00:44:21,592
Yukimura!

479
00:44:23,093 --> 00:44:24,328
Sota Yukimura.

480
00:44:25,362 --> 00:44:28,866
-Huh?
-The boy you're looking for…

481
00:44:29,900 --> 00:44:31,068
is at our company.

482
00:44:32,236 --> 00:44:33,504
His name is Sota Yukimura.

483
00:44:59,163 --> 00:45:01,331
Yukimura, why?

484
00:45:01,398 --> 00:45:03,400
‎NEXT TIME…

485
00:45:07,971 --> 00:45:08,906
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman
